  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1145 AM CDT Sat May 16 2026\n\nLow- to mid-level ridging will continue to build across the\nSoutheast early next week which indicates continued above-normal\ntemperatures in the region through Tuesday. While we remain in\nongoing drought, there's good news in the forecast for widespread\nrain chances Tuesday night through Wednesday as an upper-level\ntrough pushes east out of the Plains. This will nudge higher\nmoisture content and forcing closer to our area and provide \nmeaningful rain chances to our dry soils. It's too early to \npredict any hazardous weather with the arrival of cold front but\nwe certainly welcome any rain we can get.",
